  "status": "SUCCESS",
  "summary": "All 515 tests pass.\n\nReading taken: only the parts of the contract not yet on this backend needed work — everything else (tracker tabs, export, estimated-override, users list/create/reset-password/status, approval-rules GET/POST, template PDF/DOCX validation with the exact \"Unsupported file format. Please upload a PDF or DOCX file.\" message) already exists and matches the contract's field spelling, so I left it alone.\n\nWhat I added:\n\n- **`PUT /api/v1/settings/approval-rules/{ruleId}`** and **`DELETE /api/v1/settings/approval-rules/{ruleId}`** (TENANT_ADMIN) — router (`app/routers/settings_approval_rules.py`), service `update_rule`/`delete_rule` with the same blank-field, numeric-threshold and duplicate Contract Type + Value Threshold guards as create (400/409), 404 for an unknown rule, and `get_by_id` / duplicate-check-excluding-self in the repository. Delete is a soft delete, so approvals already in progress keep the routing they were given; both operations append a `Approval Rule` entry to `tenant_audit_log`, and create now logs too.\n- **`PUT /api/v1/tracker/bottleneck-thresholds`** (TENANT_ADMIN) — bare JSON array of `{stage, thresholdDays}` in and out, matching the GET shape. The whole array is validated before anything is written (positive whole days only, known stage → 400), values are upserted per stage, and the change is audited. The Bottleneck tab derives its stuck flag from these rows at read time, so the flag updates immediately.\n\nAlso added `UpdateApprovalRuleRequest` / `UpdateBottleneckThresholdRequest` DTOs and 14 tests covering happy path, validation, conflict, 404, 401 and 403.",
  "files_changed": [
    "app/repositories/settings_approval_rules.py",
    "app/repositories/tracker_bottleneck.py",
    "app/routers/settings_approval_rules.py",
    "app/routers/tracker_bottleneck_thresholds.py",
